<title>DUBAI: UAE's Emaar Properties announces first project.</title>
<headline>UAE's Emaar Properties announces first project.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United Arab Emirates' new Emaar Properties on Wednesday announced that its first project would be a 170 million dirham high-rise building in Dubai.</p>
<p>&quot;This hi-tech building will be the first purpose-built commercial centre in the Middle East to connect users and suppliers of information technology in the region,&quot; it said in a statement.</p>
<p>The building, with 300,000 square feet of commercial leasing space, will be on Sheikh Zaid road and will be ready within two years, it said.</p>
<p>The project's expected rate of return is 17 percent, Emaar said.</p>
</text>
